  {
   "text": "6. ASSUMPTION — LEG-TO-RAIL: bronze tube frame WELDED at the rail corners, then mechanically fastened to the case underside from inside. Rationale: welded corners are the standard and strongest detail for tube-frame bases; pinned joints add visible fasteners and racking risk at the rail. Rail section assumed 1.0 x 0.5 rectangular bronze tube to match the 1.0 dia legs. WELDED RAIL ESCALATES TO THE HUMAN-MODELING PACKAGE (outside v1 panel-and-case geometry).",
